intro="A map reference, a seat number in a hall and a position on a screen are all described by coordinates. Coordinate geometry joins algebra with geometry: we place points on the plane and compute distances and positions with formulae. This chapter develops the distance formula and the section formula and uses them to identify shapes.",
big_questions=["How far apart are two points whose coordinates are known?", "How do we locate a point that divides a segment in a given ratio?", "How can coordinates prove a shape is a square, a rhombus or a parallelogram?"],
